window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b360-d06ba8fdec310d0e.json"]={sha256:"d06ba8fdec310d0e28b94eead074e362dbef235a6b919401298d67da2b9b7419",value:{"id":"b360","title":"架空電車線懸掛系統","titleEn":"Overhead contact-line suspension systems","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"架空電車線懸掛系統以「接觸線懸掛張力垂度與溫度補償」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。架空電車線同時是導電路徑與受拉結構，跨距、張力和支承彈性共同決定受流幾何，靜態高度並不能代表列車通過的動態接觸。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops contact-wire suspension tension sag and thermal compensation through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. An overhead contact line is both a conductor and a tension structure; span, tension and support flexibility determine current-collection geometry, while static height does not establish dynamic contact. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-power","subcategoryTitle":"牽引供電與受流","subcategoryTitleEn":"Traction power and current collection","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-power","learningTags":["rail","rail-power","power"],"architectureFamily":"rail-power","architectureNodes":[["支柱吊點","Supports and droppers"],["張力補償","Tension compensation"],["接觸導線","Contact conductor"],["受電弓力","Pantograph force"],["波動幾何","Wave geometry"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-power","labels":["支柱吊點","張力補償","接觸導線","受電弓力","波動幾何"],"labelsEn":["Supports and droppers","Tension compensation","Contact conductor","Pantograph force","Wave geometry"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。只把 w 增加百分之十，y=0.229167 m。模型邊界：均勻載重小垂度弦；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。只把 T 增加百分之十，y=110.554 m/s。模型邊界：均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m. Increasing only w with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.229167 m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded small-sag string; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s. Increasing only T with a ten-percent increase gives y=110.554 m/s. Boundary: Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b360-v16-s1","title":"跨中垂度近似與弦波傳播速度","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation & String wave speed","description":"本階段聚焦「跨中垂度近似」與「弦波傳播速度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Midspan sag approximation\" and \"String wave speed\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b360-v16-01","title":"跨中垂度近似：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「跨中垂度近似」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Midspan sag approximation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小垂度近似中跨距平方放大垂度。本模型把 w 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.229167 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻載重小垂度弦。使用張力與跨中高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨中垂度近似」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Span squared amplifies sag in the small-sag approximation. In this model, w is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.229167 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniformly loaded small-sag string. Use tension and midspan level as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Loss of tension changes static contact height; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Midspan sag approximation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨中垂度近似」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Midspan sag approximation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-01-k1","title":"跨中垂度近似","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation","text":"小垂度近似中跨距平方放大垂度。本模型把 w 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.229167 m。","textEn":"Span squared amplifies sag in the small-sag approximation. In this model, w is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨中垂度近似」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Midspan sag approximation\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度","小垂度近似中跨距平方放大垂度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height.","Span squared amplifies sag in the small-sag approximation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"小垂度近似中跨距平方放大垂度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Span squared amplifies sag in the small-sag approximation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b360-v16-02","title":"跨中垂度近似：定量估算","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨中垂度近似」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Midspan sag approximation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。只把 w 增加百分之十，y=0.229167 m。模型邊界：均勻載重小垂度弦；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m. Increasing only w with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.229167 m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded small-sag string; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以張力與跨中高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型張力計與高度尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use tension and midspan level to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。只把 w 增加百分之十，y=0.229167 m。模型邊界：均勻載重小垂度弦；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m. Increasing only w with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.229167 m. Boundary: Uniformly loaded small-sag string; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨中垂度近似」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Midspan sag approximation\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: w=10 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=w*L**2/(8*T)=0.208333 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b360-v16-03","title":"跨中垂度近似：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨中垂度近似」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Midspan sag approximation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以張力與跨中高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型張力計與高度尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「跨中垂度近似」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use tension and midspan level to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model tensiometer and height gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Midspan sag approximation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「跨中垂度近似」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻載重小垂度弦如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度造成偏離的合成觀察，以張力與跨中高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Midspan sag approximation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniformly loaded small-sag string. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height. Explain which evidence in tension and midspan level distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss of tension changes static contact height. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以張力與跨中高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型張力計與高度尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「跨中垂度近似」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use tension and midspan level to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model tensiometer and height gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Midspan sag approximation. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「跨中垂度近似」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻載重小垂度弦如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度造成偏離的合成觀察，以張力與跨中高度說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Midspan sag approximation, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniformly loaded small-sag string. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height. Explain which evidence in tension and midspan level distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨中垂度近似」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Midspan sag approximation\"?","options":["本單元以張力與跨中高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型張力計與高度尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移"],"optionsEn":["Use tension and midspan level to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以張力與跨中高度區分模型與觀察，先用模型張力計與高度尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use tension and midspan level to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b360-v16-04","title":"跨中垂度近似：失效診斷","titleEn":"Midspan sag approximation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨中垂度近似」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Midspan sag approximation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度。這個失效與「跨中垂度近似」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查張力與跨中高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss of tension changes static contact height. This failure and a measurement bias in Midspan sag approximation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check tension and midspan level rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用張力與跨中高度作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Loss of tension changes static contact height; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度。這個失效與「跨中垂度近似」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查張力與跨中高度，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Loss of tension changes static contact height. This failure and a measurement bias in Midspan sag approximation can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check tension and midspan level rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨中垂度近似」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Midspan sag approximation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Loss of tension changes static contact height.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss of tension changes static contact height. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b360-v16-05","title":"弦波傳播速度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"String wave speed: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「弦波傳播速度」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “String wave speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"橫波速度由張力與線密度比決定。本模型把 T 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 110.554 m/s。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度。使用脈衝傳播時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；局部附加質量會改變波傳，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「弦波傳播速度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Transverse wave speed depends on tension-to-line-density ratio. In this model, T is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 110.554 m/s. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity. Use pulse propagation time as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Local added mass changes wave propagation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “String wave speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「弦波傳播速度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “String wave speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-05-k1","title":"弦波傳播速度","titleEn":"String wave speed","text":"橫波速度由張力與線密度比決定。本模型把 T 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 110.554 m/s。","textEn":"Transverse wave speed depends on tension-to-line-density ratio. In this model, T is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「弦波傳播速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"String wave speed\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化","橫波速度由張力與線密度比決定。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","Transverse wave speed depends on tension-to-line-density ratio."],"answer":2,"explanation":"橫波速度由張力與線密度比決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Transverse wave speed depends on tension-to-line-density ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b360-v16-06","title":"弦波傳播速度：定量估算","titleEn":"String wave speed: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「弦波傳播速度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “String wave speed” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。只把 T 增加百分之十，y=110.554 m/s。模型邊界：均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s. Increasing only T with a ten-percent increase gives y=110.554 m/s. Boundary: Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以脈衝傳播時間區分模型與觀察，先用兩點位移與高速時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use pulse propagation time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。只把 T 增加百分之十，y=110.554 m/s。模型邊界：均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s. Increasing only T with a ten-percent increase gives y=110.554 m/s. Boundary: Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「弦波傳播速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"String wave speed\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m；y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: T=15000 N, mu=1.35 kg/m; y=sqrt(T/mu)=105.409 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b360-v16-07","title":"弦波傳播速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"String wave speed: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「弦波傳播速度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “String wave speed” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以脈衝傳播時間區分模型與觀察，先用兩點位移與高速時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「弦波傳播速度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use pulse propagation time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using two-point displacement and fast timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by String wave speed. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「弦波傳播速度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由局部附加質量會改變波傳造成偏離的合成觀察，以脈衝傳播時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for String wave speed, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation. Explain which evidence in pulse propagation time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：局部附加質量會改變波傳。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Local added mass changes wave propagation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以脈衝傳播時間區分模型與觀察，先用兩點位移與高速時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「弦波傳播速度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use pulse propagation time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using two-point displacement and fast timestamps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by String wave speed. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「弦波傳播速度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻柔弦無彎曲剛度如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由局部附加質量會改變波傳造成偏離的合成觀察，以脈衝傳播時間說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for String wave speed, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform flexible string without bending rigidity. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation. Explain which evidence in pulse propagation time distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「弦波傳播速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"String wave speed\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以脈衝傳播時間區分模型與觀察，先用兩點位移與高速時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use pulse propagation time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以脈衝傳播時間區分模型與觀察，先用兩點位移與高速時間戳建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use pulse propagation time to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b360-v16-08","title":"弦波傳播速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"String wave speed: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「弦波傳播速度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “String wave speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"局部附加質量會改變波傳。這個失效與「弦波傳播速度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查脈衝傳播時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Local added mass changes wave propagation. This failure and a measurement bias in String wave speed can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check pulse propagation time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用脈衝傳播時間作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；局部附加質量會改變波傳，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local added mass changes wave propagation; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"局部附加質量會改變波傳。這個失效與「弦波傳播速度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查脈衝傳播時間，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Local added mass changes wave propagation. This failure and a measurement bias in String wave speed can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check pulse propagation time rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「弦波傳播速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"String wave speed\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化","局部附加質量會改變波傳。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","Local added mass changes wave propagation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"局部附加質量會改變波傳。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Local added mass changes wave propagation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b360-v16-s2","title":"接觸線熱伸長與吊弦名義間距","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion & Nominal dropper spacing","description":"本階段聚焦「接觸線熱伸長」與「吊弦名義間距」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Contact-wire thermal expansion\" and \"Nominal dropper spacing\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b360-v16-09","title":"接觸線熱伸長：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「接觸線熱伸長」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Contact-wire thermal expansion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長導線的熱伸長需要張力補償行程。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.561 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均溫自由熱伸長。使用線溫與補償位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「接觸線熱伸長」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Thermal growth of a long conductor consumes compensation travel. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.561 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform-temperature free expansion. Use wire temperature and compensator position as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contact-wire thermal expansion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「接觸線熱伸長」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Contact-wire thermal expansion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-09-k1","title":"接觸線熱伸長","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion","text":"長導線的熱伸長需要張力補償行程。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.561 m。","textEn":"Thermal growth of a long conductor consumes compensation travel. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「接觸線熱伸長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Contact-wire thermal expansion\" is correct?","options":["長導線的熱伸長需要張力補償行程。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差"],"optionsEn":["Thermal growth of a long conductor consumes compensation travel.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"長導線的熱伸長需要張力補償行程。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Thermal growth of a long conductor consumes compensation travel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b360-v16-10","title":"接觸線熱伸長：定量估算","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「接觸線熱伸長」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Contact-wire thermal expansion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.561 m。模型邊界：均溫自由熱伸長；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.561 m. Boundary: Uniform-temperature free expansion; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以線溫與補償位置區分模型與觀察，先用線溫計與補償行程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use wire temperature and compensator position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.561 m。模型邊界：均溫自由熱伸長；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.561 m. Boundary: Uniform-temperature free expansion; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「接觸線熱伸長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Contact-wire thermal expansion\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.000017 1/K, L=1000 m, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.51 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b360-v16-11","title":"接觸線熱伸長：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「接觸線熱伸長」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Contact-wire thermal expansion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以線溫與補償位置區分模型與觀察，先用線溫計與補償行程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸線熱伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use wire temperature and compensator position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using wire thermometer and compensator travel gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-wire thermal expansion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「接觸線熱伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫自由熱伸長如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化造成偏離的合成觀察，以線溫與補償位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-wire thermal expansion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature free expansion. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. Explain which evidence in wire temperature and compensator position distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以線溫與補償位置區分模型與觀察，先用線溫計與補償行程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「接觸線熱伸長」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use wire temperature and compensator position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using wire thermometer and compensator travel gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Contact-wire thermal expansion. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「接觸線熱伸長」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫自由熱伸長如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化造成偏離的合成觀察，以線溫與補償位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Contact-wire thermal expansion, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature free expansion. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. Explain which evidence in wire temperature and compensator position distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「接觸線熱伸長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Contact-wire thermal expansion\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移","本單元以線溫與補償位置區分模型與觀察，先用線溫計與補償行程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.","Use wire temperature and compensator position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以線溫與補償位置區分模型與觀察，先用線溫計與補償行程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use wire temperature and compensator position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b360-v16-12","title":"接觸線熱伸長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Contact-wire thermal expansion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「接觸線熱伸長」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Contact-wire thermal expansion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化。這個失效與「接觸線熱伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查線溫與補償位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-wire thermal expansion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wire temperature and compensator position rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用線溫與補償位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化。這個失效與「接觸線熱伸長」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查線溫與補償位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. This failure and a measurement bias in Contact-wire thermal expansion can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wire temperature and compensator position rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「接觸線熱伸長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Contact-wire thermal expansion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差"],"optionsEn":["A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b360-v16-13","title":"吊弦名義間距：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Nominal dropper spacing: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「吊弦名義間距」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Nominal dropper spacing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"間距分配需區分吊點數與區間數。本模型把 L 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.5 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。等間距教學配置。使用吊點里程清單作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「吊弦名義間距」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Spacing requires distinguishing support count from interval count. In this model, L is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 5.5 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Equally spaced teaching layout. Use dropper chainage list as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Confusing points and intervals causes placement error; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Nominal dropper spacing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=50 m, intervals=10 count；y=L/intervals=5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=50 m, intervals=10 count; y=L/intervals=5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「吊弦名義間距」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Nominal dropper spacing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-13-k1","title":"吊弦名義間距","titleEn":"Nominal dropper spacing","text":"間距分配需區分吊點數與區間數。本模型把 L 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.5 m。","textEn":"Spacing requires distinguishing support count from interval count. In this model, L is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「吊弦名義間距」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Nominal dropper spacing\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差","間距分配需區分吊點數與區間數。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error.","Spacing requires distinguishing support count from interval count.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"間距分配需區分吊點數與區間數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Spacing requires distinguishing support count from interval count. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b360-v16-14","title":"吊弦名義間距：定量估算","titleEn":"Nominal dropper spacing: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「吊弦名義間距」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Nominal dropper spacing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=50 m, intervals=10 count；y=L/intervals=5 m。只把 L 增加百分之十，y=5.5 m。模型邊界：等間距教學配置；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=50 m, intervals=10 count; y=L/intervals=5 m. Increasing only L with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.5 m. Boundary: Equally spaced teaching layout; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以吊點里程清單區分模型與觀察，先用尺度模型與里程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use dropper chainage list to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=50 m, intervals=10 count；y=L/intervals=5 m。只把 L 增加百分之十，y=5.5 m。模型邊界：等間距教學配置；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=50 m, intervals=10 count; y=L/intervals=5 m. Increasing only L with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.5 m. Boundary: Equally spaced teaching layout; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「吊弦名義間距」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Nominal dropper spacing\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=50 m, intervals=10 count；y=L/intervals=5 m。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=50 m, intervals=10 count; y=L/intervals=5 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：L=50 m, intervals=10 count；y=L/intervals=5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: L=50 m, intervals=10 count; y=L/intervals=5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b360-v16-15","title":"吊弦名義間距：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Nominal dropper spacing: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「吊弦名義間距」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Nominal dropper spacing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以吊點里程清單區分模型與觀察，先用尺度模型與里程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「吊弦名義間距」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use dropper chainage list to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using scale model and chainage ruler, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Nominal dropper spacing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「吊弦名義間距」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等間距教學配置如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差造成偏離的合成觀察，以吊點里程清單說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Nominal dropper spacing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equally spaced teaching layout. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. Explain which evidence in dropper chainage list distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以吊點里程清單區分模型與觀察，先用尺度模型與里程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「吊弦名義間距」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use dropper chainage list to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using scale model and chainage ruler, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Nominal dropper spacing. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「吊弦名義間距」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出等間距教學配置如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差造成偏離的合成觀察，以吊點里程清單說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Nominal dropper spacing, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Equally spaced teaching layout. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. Explain which evidence in dropper chainage list distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「吊弦名義間距」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Nominal dropper spacing\"?","options":["本單元以吊點里程清單區分模型與觀察，先用尺度模型與里程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度"],"optionsEn":["Use dropper chainage list to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以吊點里程清單區分模型與觀察，先用尺度模型與里程尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use dropper chainage list to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b360-v16-16","title":"吊弦名義間距：失效診斷","titleEn":"Nominal dropper spacing: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「吊弦名義間距」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Nominal dropper spacing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差。這個失效與「吊弦名義間距」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查吊點里程清單，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. This failure and a measurement bias in Nominal dropper spacing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check dropper chainage list rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用吊點里程清單作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差。這個失效與「吊弦名義間距」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查吊點里程清單，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. This failure and a measurement bias in Nominal dropper spacing can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check dropper chainage list rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「吊弦名義間距」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Nominal dropper spacing\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Confusing points and intervals causes placement error.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing points and intervals causes placement error. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b360-v16-s3","title":"張力補償機械比與導線直流電阻","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio & Conductor DC resistance","description":"本階段聚焦「張力補償機械比」與「導線直流電阻」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Compensator force ratio\" and \"Conductor DC resistance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b360-v16-17","title":"張力補償機械比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「張力補償機械比」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Compensator force ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想滑輪比改變力與行程的交換。本模型把 weight 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16500 N。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。無摩擦準靜態滑輪。使用重錘位移與線端位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「張力補償機械比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Ideal pulley ratio trades force against travel. In this model, weight is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 16500 N. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Frictionless quasistatic pulley. Use counterweight and wire-end movements as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Compensator force ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1；y=weight*ratio=15000 N。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1; y=weight*ratio=15000 N.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「張力補償機械比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Compensator force ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-17-k1","title":"張力補償機械比","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio","text":"理想滑輪比改變力與行程的交換。本模型把 weight 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 16500 N。","textEn":"Ideal pulley ratio trades force against travel. In this model, weight is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「張力補償機械比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Compensator force ratio\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","理想滑輪比改變力與行程的交換。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","Ideal pulley ratio trades force against travel."],"answer":2,"explanation":"理想滑輪比改變力與行程的交換。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Ideal pulley ratio trades force against travel. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b360-v16-18","title":"張力補償機械比：定量估算","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「張力補償機械比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Compensator force ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1；y=weight*ratio=15000 N。只把 weight 增加百分之十，y=16500 N。模型邊界：無摩擦準靜態滑輪；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1; y=weight*ratio=15000 N. Increasing only weight with a ten-percent increase gives y=16500 N. Boundary: Frictionless quasistatic pulley; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以重錘位移與線端位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載滑輪與力計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use counterweight and wire-end movements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1；y=weight*ratio=15000 N。只把 weight 增加百分之十，y=16500 N。模型邊界：無摩擦準靜態滑輪；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1; y=weight*ratio=15000 N. Increasing only weight with a ten-percent increase gives y=16500 N. Boundary: Frictionless quasistatic pulley; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「張力補償機械比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Compensator force ratio\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1；y=weight*ratio=15000 N。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1; y=weight*ratio=15000 N.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1；y=weight*ratio=15000 N。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: weight=5000 N, ratio=3 1; y=weight*ratio=15000 N. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b360-v16-19","title":"張力補償機械比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「張力補償機械比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Compensator force ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以重錘位移與線端位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載滑輪與力計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「張力補償機械比」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use counterweight and wire-end movements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load pulley and force gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Compensator force ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「張力補償機械比」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出無摩擦準靜態滑輪如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值造成偏離的合成觀察，以重錘位移與線端位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Compensator force ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Frictionless quasistatic pulley. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. Explain which evidence in counterweight and wire-end movements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以重錘位移與線端位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載滑輪與力計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「張力補償機械比」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use counterweight and wire-end movements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load pulley and force gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Compensator force ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「張力補償機械比」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出無摩擦準靜態滑輪如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值造成偏離的合成觀察，以重錘位移與線端位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Compensator force ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Frictionless quasistatic pulley. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. Explain which evidence in counterweight and wire-end movements distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「張力補償機械比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Compensator force ratio\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以重錘位移與線端位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載滑輪與力計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use counterweight and wire-end movements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以重錘位移與線端位移區分模型與觀察，先用低載滑輪與力計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use counterweight and wire-end movements to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b360-v16-20","title":"張力補償機械比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Compensator force ratio: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「張力補償機械比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Compensator force ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值。這個失效與「張力補償機械比」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查重錘位移與線端位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. This failure and a measurement bias in Compensator force ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check counterweight and wire-end movements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用重錘位移與線端位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值。這個失效與「張力補償機械比」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查重錘位移與線端位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. This failure and a measurement bias in Compensator force ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check counterweight and wire-end movements rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「張力補償機械比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Compensator force ratio\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension."],"answer":2,"explanation":"摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b360-v16-21","title":"導線直流電阻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conductor DC resistance: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「導線直流電阻」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conductor DC resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電阻由材料電阻率與長度面積比決定。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.157667 ohm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均溫直流均勻斷面。使用導線溫度與四線電阻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；磨耗減面積會提高電阻，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導線直流電阻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Resistance depends on resistivity and length-to-area ratio. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.157667 ohm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform-temperature DC conductor with constant area. Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Wear-reduced area raises resistance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conductor DC resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2；y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2; y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導線直流電阻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conductor DC resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-21-k1","title":"導線直流電阻","titleEn":"Conductor DC resistance","text":"電阻由材料電阻率與長度面積比決定。本模型把 rho 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.157667 ohm。","textEn":"Resistance depends on resistivity and length-to-area ratio. In this model, rho is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導線直流電阻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conductor DC resistance\" is correct?","options":["電阻由材料電阻率與長度面積比決定。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗"],"optionsEn":["Resistance depends on resistivity and length-to-area ratio.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電阻由材料電阻率與長度面積比決定。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Resistance depends on resistivity and length-to-area ratio. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b360-v16-22","title":"導線直流電阻：定量估算","titleEn":"Conductor DC resistance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導線直流電阻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conductor DC resistance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2；y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=0.157667 ohm。模型邊界：均溫直流均勻斷面；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2; y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.157667 ohm. Boundary: Uniform-temperature DC conductor with constant area; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以導線溫度與四線電阻區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓四線量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2；y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm。只把 rho 增加百分之十，y=0.157667 ohm。模型邊界：均溫直流均勻斷面；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2; y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm. Increasing only rho with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.157667 ohm. Boundary: Uniform-temperature DC conductor with constant area; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導線直流電阻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conductor DC resistance\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2; y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2；y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: rho=0.0000000172 ohm*m, L=1000 m, A=0.00012 m2; y=rho*L/A=0.143333 ohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b360-v16-23","title":"導線直流電阻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conductor DC resistance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導線直流電阻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conductor DC resistance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以導線溫度與四線電阻區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓四線量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「導線直流電阻」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using isolated low-voltage four-wire measurement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Conductor DC resistance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「導線直流電阻」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫直流均勻斷面如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由磨耗減面積會提高電阻造成偏離的合成觀察，以導線溫度與四線電阻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Conductor DC resistance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature DC conductor with constant area. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance. Explain which evidence in wire temperature and four-terminal resistance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：磨耗減面積會提高電阻。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wear-reduced area raises resistance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以導線溫度與四線電阻區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓四線量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「導線直流電阻」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using isolated low-voltage four-wire measurement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Conductor DC resistance. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「導線直流電阻」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均溫直流均勻斷面如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由磨耗減面積會提高電阻造成偏離的合成觀察，以導線溫度與四線電阻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Conductor DC resistance, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform-temperature DC conductor with constant area. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance. Explain which evidence in wire temperature and four-terminal resistance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導線直流電阻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conductor DC resistance\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化","本單元以導線溫度與四線電阻區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓四線量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以導線溫度與四線電阻區分模型與觀察，先用隔離低壓四線量測建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use wire temperature and four-terminal resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b360-v16-24","title":"導線直流電阻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conductor DC resistance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導線直流電阻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conductor DC resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"磨耗減面積會提高電阻。這個失效與「導線直流電阻」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查導線溫度與四線電阻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wear-reduced area raises resistance. This failure and a measurement bias in Conductor DC resistance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wire temperature and four-terminal resistance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用導線溫度與四線電阻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；磨耗減面積會提高電阻，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wear-reduced area raises resistance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"磨耗減面積會提高電阻。這個失效與「導線直流電阻」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查導線溫度與四線電阻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Wear-reduced area raises resistance. This failure and a measurement bias in Conductor DC resistance can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wire temperature and four-terminal resistance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導線直流電阻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conductor DC resistance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["磨耗減面積會提高電阻。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗"],"optionsEn":["Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple."],"answer":0,"explanation":"磨耗減面積會提高電阻。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wear-reduced area raises resistance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b360-v16-s4","title":"導線焦耳損耗與風載橫向位移","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss & Wind-load lateral displacement","description":"本階段聚焦「導線焦耳損耗」與「風載橫向位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Conductor Joule loss\" and \"Wind-load lateral displacement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b360-v16-25","title":"導線焦耳損耗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「導線焦耳損耗」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Conductor Joule loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電流平方造成導線熱損耗。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 19.36 kW。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。固定電阻與有效值電流。使用電流均方與電阻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導線焦耳損耗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Current squared produces conductor heating. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 19.36 kW. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Fixed resistance and RMS current. Use mean-square current and resistance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Average current understates loss under ripple; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conductor Joule loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm；y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm; y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「導線焦耳損耗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conductor Joule loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-25-k1","title":"導線焦耳損耗","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss","text":"電流平方造成導線熱損耗。本模型把 I 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 19.36 kW。","textEn":"Current squared produces conductor heating. In this model, I is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「導線焦耳損耗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Conductor Joule loss\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗","電流平方造成導線熱損耗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple.","Current squared produces conductor heating.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"電流平方造成導線熱損耗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Current squared produces conductor heating. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b360-v16-26","title":"導線焦耳損耗：定量估算","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「導線焦耳損耗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Conductor Joule loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm；y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=19.36 kW。模型邊界：固定電阻與有效值電流；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm; y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=19.36 kW. Boundary: Fixed resistance and RMS current; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以電流均方與電阻區分模型與觀察，先用合成有效值電流記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use mean-square current and resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm；y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW。只把 I 增加百分之十，y=19.36 kW。模型邊界：固定電阻與有效值電流；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm; y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW. Increasing only I with a ten-percent increase gives y=19.36 kW. Boundary: Fixed resistance and RMS current; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「導線焦耳損耗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Conductor Joule loss\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm；y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm; y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm；y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: I=400 A, R=0.1 ohm; y=I**2*R/1000=16 kW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b360-v16-27","title":"導線焦耳損耗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「導線焦耳損耗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Conductor Joule loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以電流均方與電阻區分模型與觀察，先用合成有效值電流記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「導線焦耳損耗」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use mean-square current and resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic RMS current record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Conductor Joule loss. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「導線焦耳損耗」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定電阻與有效值電流如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗造成偏離的合成觀察，以電流均方與電阻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Conductor Joule loss, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed resistance and RMS current. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Average current understates loss under ripple. Explain which evidence in mean-square current and resistance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Average current understates loss under ripple. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以電流均方與電阻區分模型與觀察，先用合成有效值電流記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「導線焦耳損耗」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use mean-square current and resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic RMS current record, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Conductor Joule loss. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「導線焦耳損耗」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出固定電阻與有效值電流如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗造成偏離的合成觀察，以電流均方與電阻說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Conductor Joule loss, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Fixed resistance and RMS current. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Average current understates loss under ripple. Explain which evidence in mean-square current and resistance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「導線焦耳損耗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Conductor Joule loss\"?","options":["本單元以電流均方與電阻區分模型與觀察，先用合成有效值電流記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差"],"optionsEn":["Use mean-square current and resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以電流均方與電阻區分模型與觀察，先用合成有效值電流記錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use mean-square current and resistance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b360-v16-28","title":"導線焦耳損耗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Conductor Joule loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「導線焦耳損耗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Conductor Joule loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗。這個失效與「導線焦耳損耗」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查電流均方與電阻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Average current understates loss under ripple. This failure and a measurement bias in Conductor Joule loss can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check mean-square current and resistance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用電流均方與電阻作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Average current understates loss under ripple; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗。這個失效與「導線焦耳損耗」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查電流均方與電阻，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Average current understates loss under ripple. This failure and a measurement bias in Conductor Joule loss can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check mean-square current and resistance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「導線焦耳損耗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Conductor Joule loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Average current understates loss under ripple.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement."],"answer":1,"explanation":"脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Average current understates loss under ripple. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b360-v16-29","title":"風載橫向位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Wind-load lateral displacement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「風載橫向位移」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wind-load lateral displacement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"小位移下橫風分布力使導線偏移。本模型把 q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.183333 m。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。靜態均布橫載小位移。使用風速與橫向位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風載橫向位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distributed crosswind force displaces the wire at small deflection. In this model, q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.183333 m. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Static uniform lateral load at small displacement. Use wind speed and lateral position as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wind-load lateral displacement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風載橫向位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wind-load lateral displacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-29-k1","title":"風載橫向位移","titleEn":"Wind-load lateral displacement","text":"小位移下橫風分布力使導線偏移。本模型把 q 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.183333 m。","textEn":"Distributed crosswind force displaces the wire at small deflection. In this model, q is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「風載橫向位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Wind-load lateral displacement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格","小位移下橫風分布力使導線偏移。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","Distributed crosswind force displaces the wire at small deflection."],"answer":2,"explanation":"小位移下橫風分布力使導線偏移。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distributed crosswind force displaces the wire at small deflection. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b360-v16-30","title":"風載橫向位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Wind-load lateral displacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風載橫向位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wind-load lateral displacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m。只把 q 增加百分之十，y=0.183333 m。模型邊界：靜態均布橫載小位移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m. Increasing only q with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.183333 m. Boundary: Static uniform lateral load at small displacement; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以風速與橫向位置區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫載與位移尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use wind speed and lateral position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m。只把 q 增加百分之十，y=0.183333 m。模型邊界：靜態均布橫載小位移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m. Increasing only q with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.183333 m. Boundary: Static uniform lateral load at small displacement; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「風載橫向位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Wind-load lateral displacement\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N；y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: q=8 N/m, L=50 m, T=15000 N; y=q*L**2/(8*T)=0.166667 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b360-v16-31","title":"風載橫向位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Wind-load lateral displacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風載橫向位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Wind-load lateral displacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以風速與橫向位置區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫載與位移尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「風載橫向位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use wind speed and lateral position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model lateral load and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Wind-load lateral displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「風載橫向位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出靜態均布橫載小位移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以風速與橫向位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Wind-load lateral displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Static uniform lateral load at small displacement. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. Explain which evidence in wind speed and lateral position distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以風速與橫向位置區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫載與位移尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「風載橫向位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use wind speed and lateral position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model lateral load and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Wind-load lateral displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「風載橫向位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出靜態均布橫載小位移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移造成偏離的合成觀察，以風速與橫向位置說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Wind-load lateral displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Static uniform lateral load at small displacement. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. Explain which evidence in wind speed and lateral position distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「風載橫向位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Wind-load lateral displacement\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以風速與橫向位置區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫載與位移尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use wind speed and lateral position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以風速與橫向位置區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫載與位移尺建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use wind speed and lateral position to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b360-v16-32","title":"風載橫向位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Wind-load lateral displacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風載橫向位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Wind-load lateral displacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移。這個失效與「風載橫向位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查風速與橫向位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. This failure and a measurement bias in Wind-load lateral displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wind speed and lateral position rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用風速與橫向位置作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移。這個失效與「風載橫向位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查風速與橫向位置，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. This failure and a measurement bias in Wind-load lateral displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check wind speed and lateral position rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「風載橫向位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Wind-load lateral displacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格","陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"陣風動態不可只用靜態偏移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Gust dynamics cannot be reduced to static displacement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b360-v16-s5","title":"受流相對速度比與懸掛點彈性位移","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio & Suspension-point elastic movement","description":"本階段聚焦「受流相對速度比」與「懸掛點彈性位移」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Collection speed ratio\" and \"Suspension-point elastic movement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b360-v16-33","title":"受流相對速度比：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「受流相對速度比」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Collection speed ratio” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"列車速度接近波速時動態耦合更需細查。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.733333 1。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻弦特徵速度比較。使用車速與獨立波速估計作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一速度比不能保證受流合格，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「受流相對速度比」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dynamic coupling needs closer study as train speed approaches wave speed. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.733333 1. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Characteristic-speed comparison for a uniform string. Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Collection speed ratio” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s；y=v/c=0.666667 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s; y=v/c=0.666667 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「受流相對速度比」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Collection speed ratio”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-33-k1","title":"受流相對速度比","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio","text":"列車速度接近波速時動態耦合更需細查。本模型把 v 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.733333 1。","textEn":"Dynamic coupling needs closer study as train speed approaches wave speed. In this model, v is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「受流相對速度比」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Collection speed ratio\" is correct?","options":["列車速度接近波速時動態耦合更需細查。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移"],"optionsEn":["Dynamic coupling needs closer study as train speed approaches wave speed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列車速度接近波速時動態耦合更需細查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dynamic coupling needs closer study as train speed approaches wave speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b360-v16-34","title":"受流相對速度比：定量估算","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「受流相對速度比」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Collection speed ratio” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s；y=v/c=0.666667 1。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.733333 1。模型邊界：均勻弦特徵速度比較；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s; y=v/c=0.666667 1. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.733333 1. Boundary: Characteristic-speed comparison for a uniform string; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以車速與獨立波速估計區分模型與觀察，先用合成速度與弦脈衝紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s；y=v/c=0.666667 1。只把 v 增加百分之十，y=0.733333 1。模型邊界：均勻弦特徵速度比較；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s; y=v/c=0.666667 1. Increasing only v with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.733333 1. Boundary: Characteristic-speed comparison for a uniform string; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「受流相對速度比」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Collection speed ratio\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：局部附加質量會改變波傳","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s；y=v/c=0.666667 1。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：點數與間隔數混淆造成定位誤差"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Local added mass changes wave propagation.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s; y=v/c=0.666667 1.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Confusing points and intervals causes placement error."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s；y=v/c=0.666667 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: v=80 m/s, c=120 m/s; y=v/c=0.666667 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b360-v16-35","title":"受流相對速度比：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「受流相對速度比」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Collection speed ratio” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以車速與獨立波速估計區分模型與觀察，先用合成速度與弦脈衝紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「受流相對速度比」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic speed and string-pulse records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Collection speed ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「受流相對速度比」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻弦特徵速度比較如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一速度比不能保證受流合格造成偏離的合成觀察，以車速與獨立波速估計說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Collection speed ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Characteristic-speed comparison for a uniform string. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. Explain which evidence in train speed and independent wave-speed estimate distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：單一速度比不能保證受流合格。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以車速與獨立波速估計區分模型與觀察，先用合成速度與弦脈衝紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「受流相對速度比」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic speed and string-pulse records, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Collection speed ratio. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「受流相對速度比」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻弦特徵速度比較如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由單一速度比不能保證受流合格造成偏離的合成觀察，以車速與獨立波速估計說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Collection speed ratio, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Characteristic-speed comparison for a uniform string. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. Explain which evidence in train speed and independent wave-speed estimate distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「受流相對速度比」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Collection speed ratio\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：磨耗減面積會提高電阻","本單元以車速與獨立波速估計區分模型與觀察，先用合成速度與弦脈衝紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Wear-reduced area raises resistance.","Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以車速與獨立波速估計區分模型與觀察，先用合成速度與弦脈衝紀錄建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use train speed and independent wave-speed estimate to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b360-v16-36","title":"受流相對速度比：失效診斷","titleEn":"Collection speed ratio: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「受流相對速度比」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Collection speed ratio” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"單一速度比不能保證受流合格。這個失效與「受流相對速度比」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查車速與獨立波速估計，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. This failure and a measurement bias in Collection speed ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check train speed and independent wave-speed estimate rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用車速與獨立波速估計作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；單一速度比不能保證受流合格，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：單一速度比不能保證受流合格」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"單一速度比不能保證受流合格。這個失效與「受流相對速度比」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查車速與獨立波速估計，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. This failure and a measurement bias in Collection speed ratio can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check train speed and independent wave-speed estimate rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「受流相對速度比」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Collection speed ratio\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["單一速度比不能保證受流合格。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移"],"optionsEn":["One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement."],"answer":0,"explanation":"單一速度比不能保證受流合格。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One speed ratio cannot certify collection performance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b360-v16-37","title":"懸掛點彈性位移：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Suspension-point elastic movement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「懸掛點彈性位移」如何影響架空電車線懸掛系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Suspension-point elastic movement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Overhead contact-line suspension systems”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"支承點彈性會參與接觸線高度變化。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.5 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。線性單點支承。使用支點力位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「懸掛點彈性位移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Support elasticity contributes to contact-wire height change. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 5.5 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Linear single-point support. Use support force-displacement as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Suspension-point elastic movement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=20000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=20000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「懸掛點彈性位移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Suspension-point elastic movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-37-k1","title":"懸掛點彈性位移","titleEn":"Suspension-point elastic movement","text":"支承點彈性會參與接觸線高度變化。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 5.5 mm。","textEn":"Support elasticity contributes to contact-wire height change. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「懸掛點彈性位移」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Suspension-point elastic movement\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移","支承點彈性會參與接觸線高度變化。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.","Support elasticity contributes to contact-wire height change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承點彈性會參與接觸線高度變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Support elasticity contributes to contact-wire height change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b360-v16-38","title":"懸掛點彈性位移：定量估算","titleEn":"Suspension-point elastic movement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「懸掛點彈性位移」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Suspension-point elastic movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=20000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=5 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=5.5 mm。模型邊界：線性單點支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=20000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=5 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.5 mm. Boundary: Linear single-point support; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以支點力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型彈簧與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use support force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=20000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=5 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=5.5 mm。模型邊界：線性單點支承；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=20000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=5 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=5.5 mm. Boundary: Linear single-point support; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「懸掛點彈性位移」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Suspension-point elastic movement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：補償卡阻會讓熱伸長轉為張力變化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：摩擦使實際張力不同於理想值","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=20000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=5 mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A stuck compensator converts expansion into tension change.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Friction separates actual tension from ideal tension.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=20000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=5 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=100 N, k=20000 N/m；y=F/k*1000=5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=100 N, k=20000 N/m; y=F/k*1000=5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b360-v16-39","title":"懸掛點彈性位移：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Suspension-point elastic movement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「懸掛點彈性位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Suspension-point elastic movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以支點力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型彈簧與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「懸掛點彈性位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use support force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model spring and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Suspension-point elastic movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「懸掛點彈性位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性單點支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以支點力位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Suspension-point elastic movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear single-point support. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. Explain which evidence in support force-displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以支點力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型彈簧與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「懸掛點彈性位移」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use support force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model spring and displacement gauge, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Suspension-point elastic movement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「懸掛點彈性位移」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出線性單點支承如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移造成偏離的合成觀察，以支點力位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Suspension-point elastic movement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Linear single-point support. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. Explain which evidence in support force-displacement distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「懸掛點彈性位移」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Suspension-point elastic movement\"?","options":["本單元以支點力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型彈簧與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：脈動電流用平均值會低估損耗"],"optionsEn":["Use support force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Average current understates loss under ripple."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以支點力位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型彈簧與位移計建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use support force-displacement to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b360-v16-40","title":"懸掛點彈性位移：失效診斷","titleEn":"Suspension-point elastic movement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"prerequisiteIds":["b360-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「懸掛點彈性位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Suspension-point elastic movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移。這個失效與「懸掛點彈性位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支點力位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Suspension-point elastic movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support force-displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用支點力位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b360-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移。這個失效與「懸掛點彈性位移」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查支點力位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Suspension-point elastic movement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check support force-displacement rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]},{"id":"b360-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「懸掛點彈性位移」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Suspension-point elastic movement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：張力下降會改變靜態接觸高度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Loss of tension changes static contact height."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把支點視為完全固定會低估動態位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Perfectly fixed supports can understate dynamic movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-energy","v16s-track-energy-guide","v16s-track-ole","v16s-track-elsafe"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b360-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b360-en.svg"}};
